@startuml GateKeeper DFD Level 1 - Top-Level Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam database {
    BackgroundColor lightblue
    BorderColor darkblue
}

title GateKeeper System - Level 1 DFD (Top-Level Processes)

actor "RAG Application" as RAG
actor "Policy Author\n(Studio)" as Author
actor "Auditor" as Auditor

rectangle "GateKeeper System" {
    
    ' Processes
    rectangle "1.0\nAuthenticate\nUser" as P1
    rectangle "2.0\nEnforce\nPolicy" as P2
    rectangle "3.0\nManage\nPolicies" as P3
    rectangle "4.0\nGenerate\nAudit Reports" as P4
    rectangle "5.0\nManage Schema\nDescriptors" as P5
    
    ' Data Stores
    database "D1\nPolicies\nDatabase" as D1
    database "D2\nSchema\nDescriptors\nDatabase" as D2
    database "D3\nAudit Log\nDatabase" as D3
    database "D4\nRedis\nCache" as D4
}

' External Entity to Process flows
RAG --> P1 : Login Credentials\n(name, password)
P1 --> RAG : JWT Token\n(tenant_id, token)

RAG --> P2 : Enforcement Request\n(stage, user, request, artifacts)
P2 --> RAG : Enforcement Response\n(decision, data, trace, policyContext)

Author --> P3 : Policy Definition\n(YAML/JSON)
P3 --> Author : Validation Results\n(errors, warnings, test results)

Author --> P5 : Schema Descriptor\n(YAML)
P5 --> Author : Descriptor Status\n(success/failure)

Auditor --> P4 : Audit Query\n(filters, timeframe)
P4 --> Auditor : Audit Report\n(decisions, traces, metrics)

' Process to Data Store flows
P2 --> D1 : Read Policies\n(stage, version)
P2 --> D2 : Read Schema\n(tenant_id, version)
P2 --> D4 : Read/Write Cache\n(user_attrs, policies)
P2 --> D3 : Write Audit Event\n(audit_id, decision, trace)

P3 --> D1 : Write Policies\n(policy, version, content)
P3 --> D1 : Read Policies\n(for validation)

P4 --> D3 : Read Audit Events\n(filtered queries)
P4 --> D4 : Read Metrics\n(counters, stats)

P5 --> D2 : Write Schema\n(tenant_id, version, descriptor)
P5 --> D2 : Read Schema\n(tenant_id, version)

P1 --> D1 : Read Tenant\n(name, password_hash)
P1 --> D4 : Cache Token\n(JWT, TTL)

    ' Inter-process flows (data flows between processes)
P2 ..> P1 : Verify Token\n(authorization header)
P1 ..> P2 : Tenant Info\n(tenant_id, name)

P3 ..> P5 : Validate Paths\n(policy paths vs schema)
P5 ..> P3 : Validation Result\n(valid/invalid paths)

note right of P2
  **Main Enforcement Process**
  - Evaluates policies
  - Executes actions
  - Builds policy context
  - Logs audit events
end note

note right of D1
  **Policies Database**
  - policies table
  - policy_versions table
  - tenants table
end note

note right of D3
  **Audit Database**
  - audit_index table
  - Decision traces
  - Metrics snapshots
end note

@enduml

